  "assumptions": [
    "PostgreSQL is the target database; uuid primary keys use gen_random_uuid() (pgcrypto/PG13+), except audit_logs which uses a bigint identity for high-volume append-only writes.",
    "All table and column names use snake_case and every table has exactly one single-column primary key; junction tables (user_roles, doctor_specialties) use a surrogate id plus a composite unique constraint on their two foreign keys.",
    "A single users table backs authentication for all roles; role-specific data lives in patients and doctors. Receptionists and administrators need no extra profile table and are identified through user_roles.",
    "A user may hold multiple roles, hence the user_roles many-to-many table; role-based access control is enforced in the application using these roles.",
    "Passwords are stored only as bcrypt hashes; verification and reset tokens are stored only as hashes in auth_tokens. JWTs are stateless and are not stored.",
    "Double-booking is prevented by pre-generated time_slots (unique doctor_id + start_time) and a partial unique index on appointments.time_slot_id for active statuses (scheduled, confirmed); booking must update the slot status within the same transaction.",
    "Weekly availability is stored as recurring rules in doctor_availability_rules and materialized into time_slots by a background job; patients search only slots with status 'open', and rule changes regenerate future open slots so changes appear within 1 minute.",
    "Cancelling an appointment sets its status to 'cancelled' and the slot back to 'open'; the 24-hour cancellation policy is enforced in application logic using time_slots.start_time. Rescheduling creates a new appointment linked via rescheduled_from_appointment_id and marks the old one 'rescheduled'.",
    "Doctor search by name uses users.first_name/last_name, by specialty uses doctor_specialties, and by department uses doctors.department_id; no-show and utilization reports are derived from appointments.status joined to time_slots by date range, so no separate report tables are needed.",
    "Each doctor belongs to exactly one department; specialties are many-to-many with doctors.",
    "Timestamps are stored in UTC; time-of-day values in availability rules are interpreted in the hospital's local time zone.",
    "Fields marked as encrypted at rest (e.g. date_of_birth, address, insurance_number, appointment reason) are encrypted via disk/column-level AES-256; the schema types remain as shown and application-level encryption may require text/bytea storage.",
    "Notifications are queued in the notifications table and sent by a worker through the email/SMS gateway; reminders are created with scheduled_at set to the appointment start minus the user's reminder_hours_before.",
    "Soft deletion is handled by status/is_active flags rather than physical deletes, to preserve appointment history and audit integrity."
  ]
